Expected elements: present

Every Must-show item renders: fixed nav with brand and resolver field; the affirmative `Real Aztec mainnet data` banner with the `aztec-mainnet` slug and the producer's sentences, inset in the content column above an aligned breadcrumb; the `Not observable` badge with the published pruning reason located in the chain's retention; full hash, `Succeeded`, and an Overview carrying block, canonicality, finality and cost; Internal calls and State changes both saying "empty permanently, not yet"; the provenance strip with all three marks drawn (heart in accent purple, not emoji), and the footer with the neutral synthetic-or-captured disclosure closing the page. No Must-not-show item appears: no debug/generate/retry affordance, no trace reference, no danger tone, no blame.

In register terms the page belongs to the 2026 web direction — light canvas, near-black type, restrained pills, monospace as texture. What breaks the belonging is the copy.

P1: the Decoded input note describes a different state than the table renders. SELECTOR is correctly em-dashed absent and RAW is empty, yet the note claims raw bytes are shown and that supplying an ABI decodes them — a remedy that cannot succeed, on the one page whose thesis is permanence.

P2s: `COST · TRANSACTIONFEE` leaks the adapter's camelCase field name where the synthetic chain says `MANA`; `transaction(s)`/`block(s)` pluralisation stubs appear three times; the banner shouts one clause in caps and defends itself twice; and its capture-strategy sentence relocates the limitation into our tooling.

Fix the ABI note first, then the label.

